From 1662c4ff1e07642566a94a8fc6f58d5652607a02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 14:00:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] Pick the key preview popup default per layout and add
 --popup

The popup is a second xdg_popup surface with its own two buffers, which a 64 MiB handheld cannot spare, while a desktop or phone layout wants it. The default therefore comes from DEFAULT_SHOW_POPUP in the layout's config header. Here the setting only decides whether the popup is drawn; the surface and its buffers are still made either way, and not making them while it is off comes with the commit that keeps the surfaces alive, which owns the popup's lifecycle. The upstream layouts keep today's value, true, and the ipaq layout will set it to false. --no-popup stays, --popup is the new inverse so either default can be overridden, and the last of the two on the command line wins. --help marks the layout's default and the man page describes both options.

With -D the binary now reports the resolved popup setting right after option parsing, so the tests can read it without a compositor. tests/check-popup.sh compares it with the macro in the layout's config header, which proves the macro reaches the binary, and checks the option order rules and the --help marker.

hide() created a wp_viewport for the popup surface in show() but never destroyed it, so every hide leaked a protocol object on the server. It is now destroyed together with the popup surface.
Upstream-Status: Pending
